# CODEOWNERS — automatic reviewer routing for the metadata_db repo.
#
# GitHub parses this file on every PR: when a changed path matches a
# rule, the listed owner(s) are auto-requested as reviewers. The LAST
# matching rule wins.
#
# Interim state: one catch-all rule owned by an individual, so every
# path in the repo routes to a real, requestable reviewer. The
# per-source team routing (repo plumbing, corpus root and venue
# registry, one rule per data-source steward folder, dual-owner rules
# for the cross-dataset mappings) is designed but deliberately not
# committed here yet: it depends on @Warehouse org team slugs that do not
# exist, and an unknown handle makes its rule silently inert — which
# would route those paths to nobody rather than falling back to the
# catch-all. The routing principles (which tier owns what, rule
# ordering, the dual-owner mappings rules) are recorded under
# "Ownership routing" in MAINTAINING.md; write the per-source rules
# here from them once the teams are provisioned and staffed.
#
# Enforcement is a branch-protection choice: with "Require review from
# Code Owners" enabled on `main`, a PR is unmergeable until an owner of
# every matched rule approves. Handles must be individual usernames or
# org teams with write access to the repo.

